Z||000000||Kwez||05-12-2001||03:33 PM||||ok, I'm pretty much decided I'll change my 86GT 3speed auto for a 88gt 5speed...<P>the prob is finding one !<BR>I thought that it was in 87 that the susp was upgraded ?<P>Is a 87GT the same mechanically as a 88 ??<P>My main 'concerns' are :<BR>1) the better / more stable susp of the 88<BR>2) the 5speed Getrag of the 88<BR>3) the better brakes of the 88<P>Is a Formula or SE or whatever model available that would be the mechanical equivalent ?<P>NB: this is a 'project' car: suspension / engine upgrade planned.<P>Thank you<BR>Phil||||reg||12
Z||000001||Fiero-Tex||05-12-2001||03:48 PM||||I don't know a whole lot about doing the swap from an auto to a 5 spd., but I do know that the 87 and 88 are completely different.  The 88 has longer control arms and vented rotors on the suspension. My 87GT has the same suspension/braking setup as the previous years.  I think that installing the 88 stuff into an older car might be harder to do, but it is a better idea if you are loking for better handling.  Good Luck!<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||ray b||05-12-2001||04:04 PM||||formula is exactly same as GT both ws6 only<BR>88 models for up grade but 4cyl is same as v6 ecp for rear roll bar and springs rates and shocks [that are long gone anyway]<BR> 88 4cyl upgraded to v6 is the cheap way to go||||reg||1
Z||000003||88formula||05-12-2001||10:45 PM||||I think everyone is missing the point here. The suspension and brakes on the 84-87 year fiero’s are the same. The suspension and brakes for the 88 fiero's are unique to that year only. In 88 there were only three model fiero’s made, GT, Formula, and coupe. The GT and Formula have the same v6 engine and WS6 suspension. The coupe had a softer suspension and a four cylinder engine. There were many more upgrades that were made to the fiero other than suspension and brakes for the 88 model year.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Kwez||05-13-2001||01:14 AM||||ok, cool that's what I wanted to know...<BR>I guess that gives me a bit more chances (of finding a car) if the Formula is equivalent to the the GT though ... even if I really prefer the GT for it's looks.<P>Would a Formula be a bit cheaper than a GT ?<BR>hehe, maybe fate wants to keep me in the 'sleeper' clan ;-)<BR>(still talking about a 5speed manual)<P>Thx people||||reg||1
